WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.180
Let’s look at the knees.

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:08.220
Knee inflammation can cause swelling, warmth, and stiffness.

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:10.490
A knee may also hurt.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:16.670
Bending the knee, using stairs, or getting out of a chair may be harder.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:21.290
Knee symptoms can have more than one cause.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:27.540
Other conditions, like osteoarthritis or gout, can also cause joint pain and swelling.

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:30.600
A picture is only a guide to the area.

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:37.360
Tell your team when the knee problem began, and whether one or both knees are affected.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:41.290
Note any swelling, and the tasks that have changed.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.800
The team may check how the knee moves, and look for other causes.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:52.890
Low-impact activities, like cycling or swimming, may help. Ask your team first.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:59.410
Get urgent medical help if symptoms are severe, or you feel very unwell.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.480
Great job! Let’s review.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.900
Knee symptoms can have more than one cause.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:09.960
A picture is only a guide to the area.
